<title>USA: VISX laser system approved for astigmatism.</title>
<headline>VISX laser system approved for astigmatism.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>VISX Inc said on Friday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration approved the use of the company's excimer laser systems for treatment of low to moderate nearsightedness with astigmatism.</p>
<p>VISX said it is the first laser manufacturer in the United States to receive such an approval. Astigmatism is a visual disorder that occurs when images are not focused at any one point on the retina.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
